<title>USA: Senetek chief scientist buys 200,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Senetek chief scientist buys 200,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>ST LOUIS, Mo. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senetck PLC said on Thursday that Gerlof Homan, its chief scientist and a director, disclosed today that he had exercised his option to buy 200,000 shares of the company's common stock.  </p>
<p>&quot;I believe Senetek's stock is tremendously undervalued given our expectations for 1997 and beyond,&quot; Homan said in a news release.</p>
<p>Senetek PLC, headquartered in London, is a medical company providing technologies and solutions for age-related health problems.</p>
<p>It's shares were unchanged at 1-9/32.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
